# Plan before writing code

Before editing or creating code, state the plan in three to five lines and wait for the user to approve it. Do not start the edits in the same turn.

The plan says what will change and what will stay the same. A question or a review needs no plan. When the user already spelled out the exact change, that message is the approval.

If you're waiting for approval before making a change, explicitly state that or ask if you can proceed with the change.
